-- Catalog of every backend renderer helper's runtime allocation and
-- ownership behaviour: one row per `*Args` record / dispatch variant across
-- prepared_backend_renderer.brp, prepared_list_renderer.brp,
-- prepared_tensor_renderer.brp, prepared_tuple_renderer.brp and
-- intrinsic_renderer.brp in stage_10_backend/. This module answers a
-- question the renderers cannot answer of themselves: what the emitted C
-- DOES at runtime once a renderer has been chosen for a Core node.
--
-- Rows were built by reading each render function's body and matching the
-- runtime function(s) it calls against blorp/src/lib/runtime/native/runtime.c
-- (see the docstring on each BackendHelperKind variant for the cited
-- function). Where a variant carries a secondary flag that changes runtime
-- behaviour (element-release policy, dict-key release policy, channel
-- send/recv runtime), it is split into its own row rather than a boolean
-- field, matching the rule the renderers already apply to list handoff
-- store/borrow variants.
--
-- This catalog is total today, but that is not the same as executable
-- coverage: allocation_report.brp reports backend_plan_coverage and
-- behavior_configuration_coverage as "catalog_only" until every rendered
-- helper in emit.brp is tagged with the BackendHelperKind it renders and the
-- allocation analysis reads backend_helper_contract for it -- only then does
-- coverage become "complete".
import:
	allocation_contracts:
		AllocationRiskReason(
			CapacityGrowthAllocation,
			CowFallbackAllocation,
			ManagedObjectAllocation,
			RuntimeOperationAllocation,
		),


record BackendHelperContract {
	allocates: List[AllocationRiskReason],
	retains: Bool,
	releases: Bool,
	calls_user_code: Bool,
	cleanup_scratch: Bool
}


--- The result of dispatching one prepared backend/list/tensor/tuple/intrinsic
--- op through its renderer: the emitted C text plus the `BackendHelperKind`
--- that C came from. Every dispatcher (`render_prepared_backend_op`,
--- `render_prepared_list_op`, `render_prepared_tensor_op`,
--- `render_prepared_tuple_op`, `render_intrinsic`) returns this instead of a
--- bare `String` so that `emit.brp`'s call sites can record which helper
--- kind produced each piece of C without re-deriving it from the op again.
--- Renderer-internal recursive calls (e.g. `render_dict_iter_header`
--- composing `BackendDictIterSourceBinding` + `BackendDictIterLoopOpen`) use
--- only `.c` from the nested `RenderedHelper` and drop `.kind`: only the
--- `emit.brp` call site for the composite op (e.g. `BackendDictIterHeader`)
--- records a kind, so nested renders are not double-counted.
record RenderedHelper {
	kind: BackendHelperKind,
	c: String
}


-- One variant per distinct emitted-C helper shape across the five stage_10_backend
-- renderer files: 98 from prepared_backend_renderer.brp (including four
-- variants added to route emit.brp's former direct blorp_alloc/
-- blorp_string_create call sites through the renderer -- see the commit
-- that added them),
-- 53 from prepared_list_renderer.brp (including one added for the same
-- reason, ListAllocWithReleaseStatements), 72 from
-- prepared_tensor_renderer.brp, 7 from prepared_tuple_renderer.brp,
-- and 153 from intrinsic_renderer.brp's
-- NoArg/OneArg/TwoArg/ThreeArg intrinsic tables (383 total). A new
-- renderer variant must be added here or backend_helper_contract's match
-- stops being exhaustive and the build fails closed.
